                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course takes the theoretical knowledge of dental implantology as its main thread and is guided by clinical diagnostic and therapeutic principle in dentistry. Spanning multiple disciplines and perspectives, including prosthodontics, dental materials, oral surgery, and periodontology. This course is going to deliver an accurate, systematic, and comprehensive exposition on the characteristics, indications, and key considerations in the application of dental implant treatment from theory to clinical practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
